From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wgpu-core: a group left out of a pipeline layout rebinds
 those after it

A pipeline layout may leave a group out (None); Vulkan then has an empty
set layout at that set. Going from a pipeline whose layout has a group
there to one without it, the binder kept the groups after it bound,
though they were bound with the old pipeline layout, which is no longer
compatible with the new one from that set on: the draws ran with those
sets disturbed (VUID-vkCmdDraw-None-08600 and VUID-vkCmdDrawIndexed-None-
08600, "statically uses descriptor set 3 ... out of bounds for the number
of sets bound (3)", on a Pixel 8a). Such a change now rebinds the groups
after it, as a group whose layout changed does.
---
diff --git a/src/command/bind.rs b/src/command/bind.rs
index ba4f93b..d3c916e 100644
--- a/src/command/bind.rs
+++ b/src/command/bind.rs
@@ -247,7 +247,11 @@ mod compat {
                 let (must_set, must_rebind) = match (&mut e.expected, new_expected_bgl) {
                     (None, None) => (false, false),
                     (None, Some(_)) => (true, true),
-                    (Some(_), None) => (true, false),
+                    // A group the new layout leaves out still changes it
+                    // there (Vulkan puts an empty set layout in the gap):
+                    // sets bound after it with the old layout are no longer
+                    // compatible with the new one, and are set again.
+                    (Some(_), None) => (true, true),
                     (Some(old_expected_bgl), Some(new_expected_bgl)) => {
                         let is_different = !old_expected_bgl.is_equal(new_expected_bgl);
                         (is_different, is_different)
